This Halloween board (working name "halloween1") is open hardware and open source.

  Hardware   CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive (CERN-OHL-P-2.0)
             The schematics, the PCBs, the artwork, the generator scripts' design
             data, the 3D-printed parts, and the documentation of how to make them.
             Full text: LICENSE-HARDWARE.txt

  Software   MIT License (below)
             The firmware, the simulations, the host tools, the build and check
             scripts.

Both licences are permissive: you may make, sell, modify and share the board and
its derivatives, keeping the copyright and licence notices.

Third-party material:
  * Symbols, footprints and 3D models copied from the KiCad libraries are
    CC-BY-SA 4.0 with the KiCad libraries' exception: using them in a design
    does not put the design under CC-BY-SA.
  * Datasheets, and Hans Rosenberg's design checklist, are not part of this
    repository (datasheets/ and references/ are ignored by git).
  * The build tools in tools/ and mfg/ were written for GPiBridge
    (github.com/gallicchio/GPiBridge, MIT) and are reused here.

